---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import TeamBuilder from '../components/TeamBuilder';
---
<BaseLayout title="Pokémon Team Weakness Calculator | Super Pokémon Team Builder" description="Find shared Pokémon team weaknesses, type resistances, immunities and 4× damage vulnerabilities across all 18 types."><SiteHeader/><main id="main"><p class="eyebrow">SEE YOUR DEFENSIVE GAPS</p><h1>Pokémon Team Weakness Calculator</h1><p class="intro">Find shared weaknesses before they become a problem. Pick your team and compare incoming damage across all 18 types.</p><TeamBuilder focus="weakness" client:load/><section class="seo-content"><h2>How team weaknesses work</h2><p>For each attacking type, the calculator multiplies its effectiveness against each defender’s types. Charizard’s Fire/Flying typing takes 4× damage from Rock; a Ground attack cannot hit a Flying type by typing alone. A teammate that resists a shared weakness can give you a switching option.</p><h3>What the matrix means</h3><p>Each column is one teammate. Each row is an incoming attack type. Values above 1× show weakness; values below 1× show resistance. 0× means type immunity. The Weak and Resist columns summarize your team, with immunities included in resistance counts.</p><h3>Limits of type-only analysis</h3><p>Abilities such as Levitate, held items, weather, moves and Terastallization can change actual damage. This calculator does not apply them. Use the output as a starting point for a casual team, rather than a battle simulation.</p><a href="/type-coverage">Check your offensive coverage next →</a></section></main><SiteFooter/></BaseLayout>
